# The public keys @chekhovbot signs the record of a check with.
#
# One line per register: the repository the bot works on, then the key, base64
# as the record itself writes it. A record names the key it was signed with, so
# during a rotation a reader can tell which of these to check against.
#
# Verifying a record needs nothing but this file:
#
#   ed25519.Verify(key, <the "<!-- chekhov:record ... -->" line, in full>,
#                  base64decode(<the "<!-- chekhov:sig ... -->" value>))
#
# A record written before #20 opens with "<!-- chekhov:roles " instead, and
# verifies the same way: the signature covers the marker as it stands.
#
# See record-key.md. Never put a private key here - the private half lives only
# in the deployment's configuration.

codecheckers/testing-dev-register  ynujENA0gGdTDk7uIBtT42qn/abwZU3/6233YZrzgig=
codecheckers/register              (none yet: the bot does not run on the production register)
